# Foundry Procedural Generator — Cursor Rules

## Project identity

- Canonical repo: `https://github.com/EmberWolf-Games/foundry-procedural-generator.git`
- Module ID: `foundry-procedural-generator`
- Current version: see `module.json` / `docs/VERSIONING.md` (format `M.m.b.p[.release]`, dot before channel)
- **Version bumps:** increment **b** only for meaningful feature changes (resets **p** to `0`); patches increment **p** only. CI auto-bumps **p** after releases.
- Read `CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` and all files in `docs/` before substantive edits.

## Mission

Build a deterministic Foundry VTT encounter generator triggered by a designated party Token entering eligible cells on a campaign-scale exploration Scene. Generated tactical Scenes must eventually be complete, reproducible, navigable, performant, maintainable, and diagnosable.

## Platform contract

- Foundry minimum: `13.351`
- Required system: D&D 5e `5.3.3+`
- Compatibility targets: Midi QOL `13.0.57+`, Monk's Active Tile Triggers `13.06+`, Seasons & Stars `0.26.0+`
- Optional integrations must be feature-detected and must degrade safely.
- Do not claim a Foundry generation or integration version is verified without recorded testing.

## Source authority

For Foundry behavior, use official documentation:

- `https://foundryvtt.com/article/module-development/`
- `https://foundryvtt.com/api/`

Never guess API signatures or use private/underscore-prefixed Foundry methods. Isolate version differences in adapters.

## Architecture boundary

Use a functional core / Foundry shell.

Pure core and generator code:

- Receives validated plain data and explicit seeded RNG streams
- Produces serializable plans and diagnostics
- Must not access Foundry globals such as `game`, `canvas`, `Hooks`, `Scene`, `CONST`, or `fromUuid`
- Must run under Node tests

Foundry shell/adapters:

- Read Documents/settings/flags and resolve UUIDs
- Convert semantic plan values to Foundry constants
- Commit Scenes and embedded Documents in batches
- Own activation, persistence, notifications, and version compatibility
- Must not make procedural random decisions

## Determinism rules

- Store a root seed and canonical seed material for every encounter.
- Use named streams: `check`, `encounter`, `layout`, `zones`, `terrain`, `walls`, `ambience`, `creatures`, `hazards`, `loot`.
- Random draws in one stage must not perturb another stage.
- Snapshot mutable inputs, profile revisions, resolved selections, time context, retries, generator version, validation results, timings, and Document counts.
- Never introduce `Math.random()` into generation.

## Runtime authority and safety

- Only `game.users.activeGM` performs persistent generation.
- Prevent duplicate work with transient locks plus durable cell state.
- Validate plans before committing Foundry Documents.
- Batch embedded-document creation by type.
- Tag generated Scenes/Documents under `flags.foundry-procedural-generator`.
- Cleanup may delete only explicitly tagged generated content and must never delete the source exploration Scene.
- Keep Document budgets bounded; never create one Tile per floor cell.

## Integration boundaries

### Midi QOL

- Midi owns attacks, saves, damage, targeting, reactions, concentration, effects, and workflows.
- Generate standard D&D 5e Documents.
- Do not override Item use or Midi workflow internals.
- Use the narrow feature-detected adapter only for explicit automated Item use.

### Monk's Active Tile Triggers

- Never create or mutate `flags.monks-active-tiles`.
- Exploration checks are not MATT Tile triggers.
- Preserve the settled-movement debounce and authoritative Token re-read.
- Test movement, stop, redirect, teleport, pause, and chained actions.

### Seasons & Stars

- Consume read-only calendar/time context.
- Prefer `game.seasonsStars.integration.api`; feature-detect fallback APIs.
- Snapshot time context at encounter-check time.
- Do not advance time without an explicit owner-approved policy.
- Fall back safely to Foundry world time.

## Current milestone

The project is completing M1: trigger-to-Scene vertical slice. Do not begin M2 procedural layout work until M1 is proven inside Foundry.

M1 must prove:

- Module loads in target Foundry/D&D 5e versions
- One new cell produces one authoritative check
- 0% and 100% checks behave correctly
- Revisit default prevents duplicate generation
- Same seed gives same plan
- Scene and Wall Documents are valid
- Manifest, return, and cleanup behavior are safe
- Optional modules do not conflict
- Exact test versions and results are documented

## Coding rules

- Use modern plain JavaScript ES modules unless the owner approves a tooling migration.
- Keep project IDs/settings/flags/hooks centralized.
- Add tests for all pure logic.
- Preserve stored-data schema versions and add migrations for semantic changes.
- Update README, changelog, and design docs when behavior changes.
- Avoid dependencies without a documented rationale, license review, and browser impact.
- Do not commit campaign assets, credentials, campaign salts, or other secrets.
- Do not invent unresolved campaign decisions; consult `docs/campaign-decisions.md` and ask the owner.

## Before large edits

1. Run `npm test`.
2. State what is implemented versus scaffolded.
3. Identify the smallest safe change.
4. Explain determinism, persistence, compatibility, and migration impact.
5. Cite official API documentation for Foundry-specific changes.
